Apple's annual four-day <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/gifts/black-friday-event">Black Friday through Cyber Monday shopping event</a> is returning on Friday, November 27 through Monday, November 30 in many countries, including the United States, Canada, Australia, New Zealand, France, Germany, Italy, Spain, the United Kingdom, Belgium, the Netherlands, Sweden, Thailand, and others.<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/Apple-2026-Black-Friday-Event-Hero.jpg" alt="" width="1493" height="840" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1078373" /><br/>
In the U.S., Apple's <a href="https://www.apple.com/shop/gifts/black-friday-event/terms-conditions">terms and conditions</a> say the promotion begins on November 27 at 12 a.m. Pacific Time and ends on November 30 at 11:59 p.m. Pacific Time. <br/>
<br/>
During the shopping event, customers can get an Apple gift card with the purchase of an eligible product at an Apple Store, in the Apple Store app, and on Apple.com. However, the gift card can only be used towards future purchases, and higher immediate discounts on Apple products are <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/roundup/black-friday/"><strong>frequently available at Amazon</strong></a> and other resellers.<br/>
<br/>
In the U.S., Apple is offering gift cards worth up to &#36;300 with the purchase of an eligible iPhone, iPad, Mac, Apple Watch, HomePod, AirPods, Beats headphones, Beats Pill speaker, Apple Pencil Pro, and select Magic Keyboards for iPads.<br/>
<br/>
For the first time ever, Apple is also offering a &#36;25 gift card with select third-party accessories from brands including Anker, Belkin,  Mophie, Nimble, Rains, and Twelve South. The selection includes chargers and MacBook covers.<br/>
<br/>
As usual, many of Apple's newer products are excluded from the offer, including the iPhone 18 Pro, iPhone 18 Pro Max, iPhone Duo, MacBook Neo, latest models of the iPad mini, Apple TV 4K, iMac, and Mac Studio, and more. Refurbished products are also ineligible, and the offer cannot be combined with educational pricing.<br/>
<br/>
